<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea to crack down on market rumour mongers.</title>
<headline>S.Korea to crack down on market rumour mongers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Supervisory Board said on Thursday it would start cracking down on rumour mongers to protect investors and corporate activities.  </p>
<p>The board said false rumours could hurt corporate fund-raising which could damage the nation's economy.</p>
<p>Last week, Kia Group was put under the protection of its creditor banks after they determined Kia would be unable to avoid defaulting on its debt payments.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
